Moby Hyphenator II — provenance and license
============================================

mhyph.tsv.gz is derived from the Moby Hyphenator II word list (mhyph.txt,
187,175 entries) by Grady Ward, part of the Moby Project. It was cleaned and
re-encoded by tools/mkhyphdict in this repository (MacRoman -> ASCII, 0xA5
syllable separators -> '-', phrases / duplicates / corrupt lines dropped).

The Moby lexicon is in the PUBLIC DOMAIN. Grady Ward placed the Moby Project
materials in the public domain; Project Gutenberg records the grant as
"Public Domain material by grant from the author, January, 2001."

